keep-data: the old system Debian GNU/Linux 8 (jessie) on /dev/sda2; UEFI firmware; the layout of the profile is not applied, no disk is wiped or partitioned
FORMAT (what is on them is lost)
  /dev/sda2   ext4      /  (20G)
  /dev/sda5   ext4      /var/lib  (1G, was ext3)
KEEP (as they are, mounted where they were)
  /dev/sda1   vfat      /boot/efi  (the EFI system partition: not formatted, the new boot loader is added)
  /dev/md127  ext4      /home
  /dev/sda4   reiserfs  /srv/old  (reiserfs: with nofail, the new system may not be able to mount it)
ASIDE (kept, under another name)
  /dev/sda6   ext4      /var/cache -> /var/cache.old  (mounted)
LOST (on the old root, beyond the system itself)
  nothing found
WARNINGS
  /home is kept: the profile's users get their home directories and keys there; a home directory that is there already goes to the user of its name (its files change owner where the user's ID differs), its authorized_keys is replaced (the old one saved beside it)
  /dev/sda4 (/srv/old) is reiserfs, which the new system may not be able to mount: kept with nofail, so that it boots without it
